{"id":"f13d4bbe06c4eb5a","group":"58","path":"58/batch08/58-df-gch.md","title":"Generalized Continuum Hypothesis","display":"df-gch — Generalized Continuum Hypothesis","type":"definition","metadata":{"type":"definition","book":"Set Theory","book_abbrev":"58","label":"58-df-gch","aliases":["58-df-gch"],"display":"df-gch — Generalized Continuum Hypothesis","depends_on":["[[../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-aleph.md]]","[[../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md]]"]},"metadataError":null,"renderWarnings":[],"properties":[{"key":"type","html":"definition"},{"key":"book","html":"Set Theory"},{"key":"book_abbrev","html":"58"},{"key":"label","html":"58-df-gch"},{"key":"aliases","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span>58-df-gch</span></div>"},{"key":"display","html":"df-gch — Generalized Continuum Hypothesis"},{"key":"depends_on","html":"<div class=\"property-array\"><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-1\" data-note=\"949691fe1747f59d\" href=\"?note=949691fe1747f59d\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md\">../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-2\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md\">../batch17/58-df-aleph.md</a></span><span><a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-3\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a></span></div>"}],"html":"\n<h2 id=\"Hypothesis\">[Hypothesis]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{GCH}\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\">\\(\\mathrm{GCH}\\in\\{\\top,\\bot\\}\\)</span> (generalized-continuum-hypothesis proposition defined here)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ordinal}\\subseteq V\">\\(\\mathrm{Ordinal}\\subseteq V\\)</span> (ordinal predicate, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-4\" data-note=\"5582a281f15a33c2\" href=\"?note=5582a281f15a33c2\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md\">../batch17/58-df-ordinal.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\aleph_\\alpha\">\\(\\aleph_\\alpha\\)</span> (aleph notation for ordinal <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\alpha\">\\(\\alpha\\)</span>, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-5\" data-note=\"535817bf563314f5\" href=\"?note=535817bf563314f5\" title=\"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md\">../batch17/58-df-aleph.md</a>)</li>\n<li><span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"2^\\kappa\">\\(2^\\kappa\\)</span> (cardinal exponentiation, see <a class=\"wiki-link\" id=\"ref-6\" data-note=\"949691fe1747f59d\" href=\"?note=949691fe1747f59d\" title=\"../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md\">../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md</a>)</li>\n</ul>\n<h2 id=\"Assertion\">[Assertion]</h2>\n<figure class=\"equation\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gch} \\vdash \\mathrm{GCH} \\leftrightarrow \\forall \\alpha\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\to 2^{\\aleph_\\alpha}=\\aleph_{\\alpha+1}\\bigr)\"><div class=\"math-display\" tabindex=\"0\" role=\"region\" aria-label=\"数学公式\">\\[\\mathrm{df\\text{-}gch} \\vdash \\mathrm{GCH} \\leftrightarrow \\forall \\alpha\\in V\\;\\bigl(\\mathrm{Ordinal}(\\alpha)\\to 2^{\\aleph_\\alpha}=\\aleph_{\\alpha+1}\\bigr)\\]</div><button class=\"equation-action\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"展开查看完整公式\">展开公式 ↗</button></figure><h2 id=\"Remark\">[Remark]</h2>\n<ul>\n<li>Quantification is over sets satisfying the ordinal predicate; neither <span class=\"math-inline\" data-tex=\"\\mathrm{Ord}\">\\(\\mathrm{Ord}\\)</span> nor the aleph class function is treated as a set.</li>\n</ul>\n","headings":[{"id":"Hypothesis","text":"[Hypothesis]","level":2},{"id":"Assertion","text":"[Assertion]","level":2},{"id":"Remark","text":"[Remark]","level":2}],"links":[{"target":"../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md","status":"resolved","id":"949691fe1747f59d","anchor":"ref-1","targetAnchor":"","location":"元数据 · depends_on","heading":"","excerpt":"[[../batch14/58-df-cardinalexpp.md]]","embed":false},{"target":"../batch17/58-df-aleph.md","status":